WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:04.490
Hollywood has churned out some regrettable
remakes over the years, but among the garbage,

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:09.920
there have also been some successful cinematic
revivals like Ocean's Eleven and The Thing,

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:13.660
both of which made audiences forget there
was something else to compare them to in the

00:00:13.669 --> 00:00:14.669
first place.

00:00:14.669 --> 00:00:18.720
With that optimistic outlook in mind, let's
take a look at all the remakes Tinseltown

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.240
has in the works that might be worth your
ticket money.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:22.380
Suspiria

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:28.560
1977's Suspiria has been described as "a nightmare
fairytale etched in neon colors."

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:33.771
The horror film focused on an American ballerina
who arrives at a European dance academy, only

00:00:33.771 --> 00:00:38.550
to find herself in serious trouble when the
students start dying in disturbing ways.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:43.360
It's as good as Italian horror cinema gets,
and remaking it seems like an impossible task…but

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:49.160
Luca Guadagnino is going to try anyway, The
Italian filmmaker is working with an impressive

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:55.050
roster of great actresses, including Dakota
Johnson, Tilda Swinton, Chloë Grace Moretz,

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:59.970
and Mia Goth, and even Jessica Harper, the
star of the original, will make a cameo in

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:01.020
the new iteration.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.820
The biggest difference we'll see is in the
color choices involved in the remake.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:09.660
While the original is perhaps the most colorful
horror film ever put to celluloid, Guadagnino

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:12.679
says his take will have "no primary colors."

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:16.860
Instead, prepare yourself for a film that's
"winter-ish, evil, and really dark."

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:18.580
Dirty Rotten Scoundrels

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:24.740
1988's Dirty Rotten Scoundrels was a classic
comedy starring Michael Caine and Steve Martin

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:27.660
as two con men who had made a rather despicable
wager.

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:32.000
The two were trying to fleece an heiress out
of her money, and whoever lost the bet had

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:32.880
to skip town.

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:36.540
But while the film was a success, the story
was hardly original.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:42.520
Dirty Rotten Scoundrels was actually a remake
of a 1964 film called Bedtime Story, which

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:43.940
starred Marlon Brando.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:48.100
MGM is currently updating the movie again
with women in the lead instead.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:53.979
The new pic, Nasty Women, will star Anne Hathaway
and Rebel Wilson as the two despicable scammers.

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:59.030
If Nasty Women manages to bring back the whole
cultured crook versus crass con artist angle,

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:01.200
then it's not difficult to guess who will
play who.

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:03.740
"He loves to run and run and run."

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:04.440
Overboard

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:10.240
Released in 1987, Garry Marshall's Overboard
may have divided critics, but it eventually

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:12.520
won the hearts of comedy fans across the world.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:17.300
Starring the legendary couple of Kurt Russell
and Goldie Hawn, the film focused on a spoiled

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:21.060
heiress who fell off a yacht and woke up in
a hospital with amnesia.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:25.560
Through a series of hijinks, her carpenter
tricked her into thinking she was his wife

00:02:25.569 --> 00:02:27.300
and hillbilly hell broke out.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:30.140
"Why do I have this depressed look on my face
all the time?"

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:31.820
"Well, you were grumpy a lot."

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:37.220
Flash forward three decades, and Overboard
is being remade with Anna Faris and Eugenio

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:38.900
Derbez in the lead roles.

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:40.260
But this time, there's a little twist.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.940
"Surprise!"

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.920
The roles will be flipped, with Derbez playing
a selfish playboy from a wealthy Mexican family

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:53.500
who loses his memory after taking a tumble
off a boat, while Faris will be a single mom

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.120
who fools Derbez into thinking he's her husband.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.320
When in doubt, gender-swap it out.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:02:59.780
The Thomas Crown Affair

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:04.990
Coming off films like Creed and Fruitvale
Station, there's no denying Michael B. Jordan

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:07.520
is one of the most exciting actors working
today.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:12.090
Now, he'll be following in Steve McQueen's
footsteps with another adaptation of The Thomas

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:12.920
Crown Affair.

00:03:13.209 --> 00:03:18.359
The original 1968 film followed a wealthy
businessman who orchestrated a nearly perfect

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:19.340
bank robbery.

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:23.840
But eventually, an insurance investigator
began to suspect Crown of pulling off the

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:24.340
heist.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:28.819
Sparks eventually flew between them and the
two leads had to grapple with both their emotions

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:31.840
and millions of dollars as they tried to outwit
one another.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:36.740
The film was already remade with some success
with Pierce Brosnan and Rene Russo as the

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:41.209
co-leads, but what's really impressive is
that this new version is all Michael B. Jordan's

00:03:41.209 --> 00:03:41.709
idea.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:46.700
Jordan reportedly pitched MGM on the idea
for a remake himself and landed the title

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:47.900
role as a result.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:49.800
The Raid: Redemption

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:54.519
One of the craziest action movies in recent
memory, The Raid: Redemption followed a SWAT

00:03:54.519 --> 00:03:59.269
team trying to nab a notorious crime lord,
but most of the movie was made up of fantastic

00:03:59.269 --> 00:04:03.889
fight scenes as the team battles their way
up a heavily-guarded high-rise apartment building.

00:04:03.889 --> 00:04:09.050
However, while the original Raid is a martial
arts extravaganza, director Joe Carnahan plans

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:11.360
on getting grittier with his upcoming remake.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:16.580
The director of films like Narc and The Grey,
Carnahan is teaming up with actor Frank Grillo

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:21.060
to create a film he says will feel like a
feature-length version of the knife fight

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.820
scene in Saving Private Ryan.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:24.340
Death Wish

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:29.560
The quintessential revenge flick, Michael
Winner's Death Wish saw a pacifist-turned-killer

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:34.280
declare war on New York criminals after a
gang of thugs murdered his wife and raped

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:35.020
his daughter.

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:39.820
While the film stirred up quite a bit of controversy
back in the day, Death Wish was financially

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:42.160
successful enough to spawn several sequels.

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:44.400
"Hey."

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:47.300
"What's the problem?"

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:53.080
Now, over 40 years later, MGM has decided
to remake the dirty and gritty thriller and

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:54.820
possibly start a new series.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:59.600
Only this time, Bruce Willis will be playing
the part of Paul Kersey instead of Charles

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:03.240
Bronson, and Eli Roth will step behind the
camera for the flick.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:08.960
According to Roth, we can expect to see Hostel-style
torture scenes with "spectacular set pieces"

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:11.880
on this remake, so get ready to lose your
appetite.

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:16.460
"Because a death wish always comes true."

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:18.840
An American Werewolf in London

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:23.580
When it comes to werewolves, there's one film
that stands snout and shoulders above the

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:24.080
rest.

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:27.780
An American Werewolf in London is the quintessential
lycanthrope flick.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:31.960
So, Universal's upcoming remake has some pretty
big pawprints to fill.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:36.700
David Alpert and Robert Kirkman of The Walking
Dead fame are set to produce the new American

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:39.900
Werewolf, bringing some serious horror cred
to the project.

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:43.960
Meanwhile, Universal is keeping things in
the family on the filmmaking side.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:49.060
Hoping to recapture the black magic of the
original, the studio has brought out Max Landis,

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:53.680
the son of the original's writer and director,
John Landis', to pen the screenplay and helm

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:54.220
the film.

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:58.180
So, hopefully, this won't be just another
bad moon movie on the rise.

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:00.000
"Tra la la la la la.

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:01.000
Isn't this fun?"

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:03.220
The Great Outdoors

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:08.520
One of John Hughes' lesser-known scripting
efforts, The Great Outdoors was a 1988 comedy

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:13.720
starring John Candy as Chet Ripley, a Chicagoan
who just wants to spend some time with his

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:15.940
family out in the Wisconsin wilderness.

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:20.900
Unfortunately, Chet's relaxing vacation was
ruined when his annoying brother-in-law crashed

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:26.210
the party with his own family in tow, leading
to a series of escapades involving water skis,

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:28.700
a giant steak, and a bald-headed bear.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:33.640
Now, Universal Pictures is aiming to reboot
the film with Kevin Hart on board to lead.

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:38.400
Whether he plays Chet or his brother-in-law
remains to be seen, but we can count on the

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:42.590
funnyman to deliver some memorable moments
and remind everyone what an underrated gem

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:43.620
the original was.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:45.180
Scarface

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:48.440
Say hello to a little remake of this gangster
classic.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:53.690
As one of Al Pacino's most acclaimed performances,
it's no wonder fans are a bit skeptical about

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:56.840
anyone touching Brian De Palma's 1983 film.

00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:00.980
But what most people don't know is that Scarface
was actually a remake itself.

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:06.120
The first Scarface was filmed in 1932, and
it featured an Italian immigrant making a

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:08.380
name for himself in the Chicago mob.

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:12.890
A couple of decades later, De Palma simply
switched the setting to Miami, turned the

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:16.720
main character into a Cuban, and created an
all-time masterpiece.

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:21.560
In keeping with the Scarface remake tradition,
the new film will take place in Los Angeles

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:24.000
and follow a Mexican immigrant's rise to power.

00:07:24.140 --> 00:07:29.020
Diego Luna will play the main character, working
with a screenplay written by Boardwalk Empire's

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:31.760
Terence Winter and doctored by the Coen brothers.

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:36.080
You might recall that the last time the sibling
duo had anything to do with a script about

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:41.280
drugs, murder, and Mexican cartels, it worked
out pretty well, so maybe we should be optimistic

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:43.220
about Scarface's modern-day revival.

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:44.740
The Intouchables

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:50.680
When The Intouchables made its way to America
in 2012, the film was not a commercial success.

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:53.960
But overseas, this French drama made an absolute
killing.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:59.150
The story focused on the relationship between
a paralyzed man named Philippe and his Senegalese

00:07:59.150 --> 00:08:00.449
caretaker, Driss.

00:08:00.449 --> 00:08:04.720
In addition to race, the two are separated
by class and different worldviews, but over

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:09.000
the course of the film, the two form a bond
and help each other become better people.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:14.140
Now, the Weinstein Company is giving Americans
another chance to see the movie—only this

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:16.340
time, they'll get to hear all the dialogue
in English.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:21.740
Re-titled Untouchable, the upcoming remake
will star Bryan Cranston as the wheelchair-bound

00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:26.050
Philip; and, Kevin Hart will play Dell, Philip's
new assistant from the Bronx.

00:08:26.050 --> 00:08:29.140
Nicole Kidman will also star and Neil Burger
will direct.

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:32.560
The pic will bow into theaters in March, 2018.

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:34.640
Starship Troopers

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:39.750
Directed by Paul Verhoeven, Starship Troopers
has never gotten the same amount of love as

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:44.610
the director's magnum opus, RoboCop, but it's
still gained a sizable cult following over

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:45.200
the years.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:50.300
The 1997 original followed a group of kids
who join the military to fight bugs in outer

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:50.800
space.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:51.920
"BUGS.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:54.260
BUGGGGGGGS!"

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:59.700
Initially, the movie was misunderstood by
quite a few critics, but these days, Troopers

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:02.900
is widely recognized as a biting satire on
fascism.

00:09:03.070 --> 00:09:06.900
The original novel, written by Robert A. Heinlein,
couldn't be more different.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:11.240
The book has a much more pro-war stance than
the Verhoeven film, which means the upcoming

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:13.160
remake will diverge significantly.

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:17.440
Columbia Pictures hopes to bring kick off
"a potential franchise" with a new Starship

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:22.640
Troopers—but most importantly, the upcoming
version will stick a lot closer to the novel.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:23.920
Maniac Cop

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:29.760
Directed by the infamous William Lustig, 1988's
Maniac Cop has been described as "schlocky"

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:31.860
and "scummy"... and "actually kinda fun."

00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:36.700
The exploitation flick features Tom Atkins
as a cop investigating a series of murders,

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:41.680
Robert Z'Dar as a psychopathic police officer
killing anyone in his path, and Bruce Campbell

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.480
as an innocent cop caught in the middle.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:47.780
While the film wasn't exactly a critical hit,
the slasher has picked up a cult following

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:48.820
over the years.

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:54.360
The Maniac Cop remake has been in the works
since 2012, but in 2015, things really started

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:54.860
moving.

00:09:55.060 --> 00:10:00.580
Marvel and DC Comics writer Ed Brubaker is
writing the script, with John Hyams directing.

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:05.820
In March 2017, Variety reported that the film
would start shooting this summer, although

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:09.980
the remake isn't going to be exactly the same
as Lustig's original B-picture.

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:15.140
This time, Maniac Cop will be more of a realistic
thriller than a horror film, with Producer

00:10:15.140 --> 00:10:20.290
Nicolas Winding Refn telling Bloody Disgusting
the new film will "serve as more of a commentary

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:24.860
on modern day society" and the sometimes questionable
actions of law enforcement.

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:29.040
There's no word yet on who's starring, but
whoever they pick, they'll probably pale in

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:33.280
comparison to Campbell and Z'Dar…and least
when it comes to their chins, anyway.

00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:34.700
Thanks for watching!

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:37.410
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:39.779
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

